    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2 tests pass \u2014 the acceptance suite is the only test module).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `locality` as a read-only field derived from an owner's city, surfaced on both `POST /api/owners` and `GET /api/owners/{id}` responses (both serialize through `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`).\n\n**Changes:**\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `locality` property to the `Owner` schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it), documenting the fixed table and the `UNKNOWN` fallback.\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/Locality.java`** (new) \u2014 a small helper with `static String of(String city)` implementing the fixed table (`Sydney\u2192NSW`, `Melbourne\u2192VIC`, `Brisbane\u2192QLD`, else `UNKNOWN`).\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"locality\", expression = \"java(Locality.of(owner.getCity()))\")`, matching the existing derived-field pattern (`displayName`, `membershipTier`, \u2026).\n\n**Notable pitfall caught and fixed:** my first attempt put the lookup as a `default String locality(String)` method on the mapper interface. That compiled but broke `POST` with a 500 at persist time \u2014 MapStruct auto-selects any `String\u2192String` method as an implicit converter for *every* String property, so `telephone`/`city`/etc. were routed through it, leaving `telephone` non-normalized and failing the entity's E.164 `@Pattern`. Moving the logic to a standalone helper class (no String\u2192String method on the mapper) resolved it. I verified this by isolating the regression against the reverted baseline before committing to the helper-class approach.\n\nBoth `coreDerivesRegionForKnownCity` (Sydney\u2192NSW) and `functionalityUnknownCityIsUnknown` (random city\u2192UNKNOWN) pass.",
